"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T00:47:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T00:47:50Z","body":"Rebase is done. \r\n\r\nI may have made a mistake with the MRP in #103726.\r\n\r\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19406450/MRP.zip)\r\n\r\nThe issue fixed here is similar to the left and right navigation issue in the MRP above.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745940320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777650115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104017#issuecomment-2777650115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104017","id":2777650115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lj5PD","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T06:14:11Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T06:14:11Z","body":"Instead of `CanvasItem.get_screen_transform` you should use\r\n`Viewport.get_screen_transform` and `CanvasItem.get_global_transform_with_canvas`, because `CanvasItem.get_screen_transform` doesn't necessarily take you to the screen but only to the Viewports embedder.\r\nSee the graphics here: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/core_and_modules/2d_coordinate_systems.html\r\n\r\nBe aware, that this still doesn't work in all cases of a \"[GUI in 3D](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/viewport/gui_in_3d)\" setting, because there is no automatic conversion available. But there is no easy solution available, so I believe that this use-case can be ignored for now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777650115/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777702637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104017#issuecomment-2777702637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104017","id":2777702637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lkGDt","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T06:50:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T07:01:32Z","body":"> use `Viewport.get_screen_transform` and `CanvasItem.get_global_transform_with_canvas`\r\n\r\nThis still doesn't seem right for a `SubViewport` inside a `SubViewportContainer`. ~~In this case, it is still relative to the parent viewport's canvas.~~\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777702637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780100607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104017#issuecomment-2780100607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104017","id":2780100607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ltPf_","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T01:16:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T01:18:52Z","body":"Since focus search can only be performed in the same control tree, and the same transformation except `rotation` and `skew` is applied to the entire control tree, it does not affect the direction. So for 2D, `get_screen_transform()` is enough.\r\nThis can eliminate the influence of `rotation` and `skew` on the direction that may exist in the transformation of the canvas.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780100607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3143640262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104017#issuecomment-3143640262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104017","id":3143640262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67YCTG","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T08:02:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T08:02:43Z","body":"As far as I can tell, my previous comment is still valid.\r\n\r\n> Instead of `CanvasItem.get_screen_transform` you should use `Viewport.get_screen_transform` and `CanvasItem.get_global_transform_with_canvas`, because `CanvasItem.get_screen_transform` doesn't necessarily take you to the screen but only to the Viewports embedder.\r\n\r\nUsing `CanvasItem.get_screen_transform` will not work correctly in `SubViewport`s.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3143640262/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]